1
00:00:07,749 --> 00:00:10,431
This is Part 2 of 6: What it is.

2
00:00:11,233 --> 00:00:15,473
In Part 1, I asked whether the apple and
the mountain are as straightforward as

3
00:00:15,553 --> 00:00:17,471
they look. They are not.

4
00:00:17,551 --> 00:00:21,995
Dependent arising is at the centre
of almost everything I have written.

5
00:00:22,075 --> 00:00:24,540
Now I set out the view itself, whole.

6
00:00:25,362 --> 00:00:31,328
That matters, because dependent arising is
easy to agree with, and easy to mishear.

7
00:00:31,408 --> 00:00:35,038
Most people already accept that
things depend on other things.

8
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:37,039
Then they hear one of five things.

9
00:00:37,911 --> 00:00:39,054
First, a web.

10
00:00:39,134 --> 00:00:42,750
Things are unfindable, but
surely the connections are there.

11
00:00:42,830 --> 00:00:46,735
A network, a field of
relations, the floor at last.

12
00:00:47,546 --> 00:00:49,301
Second, a machine.

13
00:00:49,381 --> 00:00:52,810
Causes working in the dark,
each pushing the next.

14
00:00:53,663 --> 00:00:55,730
Third, only concepts.

15
00:00:55,810 --> 00:01:00,476
If it is designated, it is a story,
and causes are not really there.

16
00:01:01,347 --> 00:01:03,160
Fourth, a lower truth.

17
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:08,011
Fine for the world, to be left
behind when one sees the ultimate.

18
00:01:08,863 --> 00:01:11,093
Fifth, the shape of ignorance.

19
00:01:11,173 --> 00:01:16,297
The twelve links begin with ignorance, so
dependent arising must be the pattern of

20
00:01:16,377 --> 00:01:17,577
confusion.

21
00:01:18,245 --> 00:01:21,471
Each takes something true and
sets it on the wrong foot.

22
00:01:22,294 --> 00:01:25,557
So what does it say? A bell
rings when it is struck.

23
00:01:25,637 --> 00:01:27,568
A seed of rice gives rice.

24
00:01:27,648 --> 00:01:31,684
A harsh word, met with a
certain mood, brings anger.

25
00:01:31,764 --> 00:01:35,221
The order is reliable,
and actions have results.

26
00:01:36,037 --> 00:01:39,421
Dependent arising says: these conditions,

27
00:01:39,501 --> 00:01:41,962
met together, and this appears.

28
00:01:42,042 --> 00:01:43,760
Designated, and working.

29
00:01:44,574 --> 00:01:48,258
What it never says is that a
cause, standing on its own,

30
00:01:48,338 --> 00:01:51,016
makes an effect and hands it across.

31
00:01:51,096 --> 00:01:54,304
The ringing is not made
by the bronze, the strike,

32
00:01:54,384 --> 00:01:58,720
the air and the ear, and then
sent out. It is their meeting.

33
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:01,478
Nothing passes from the
strike to the sound.

34
00:02:01,558 --> 00:02:04,617
Nothing stands behind
the sound, producing it.

35
00:02:04,697 --> 00:02:07,597
Yet without the strike,
there is no ringing.

36
00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:12,203
This is what I call causal
efficacy without causal power.

37
00:02:12,283 --> 00:02:14,363
Conditions condition, fully.

38
00:02:14,443 --> 00:02:17,805
And no power is ever
found sitting in a cause.

39
00:02:18,625 --> 00:02:23,259
Conventionally, we say the strike
produces the sound, and that is fine.

40
00:02:23,339 --> 00:02:25,664
The analysis does not take it away.

41
00:02:25,744 --> 00:02:30,723
It shows only that things do not function
the way the inherent mind thinks they do.

42
00:02:31,554 --> 00:02:36,950
But when the producing cause falls away,
one part is almost always left over.

43
00:02:37,030 --> 00:02:39,559
The resounding ting is consciousness.

44
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:41,927
It is my very radiance clarity.

45
00:02:42,729 --> 00:02:44,102
This reading is fine.

46
00:02:44,182 --> 00:02:48,613
It is an important non-dual insight,
and a recognition of anatta.

47
00:02:48,693 --> 00:02:51,032
No hearer stands apart from the ting.

48
00:02:51,112 --> 00:02:52,816
The ting is the hearing.

49
00:02:53,629 --> 00:02:56,538
What I want to stress is
what tends to happen next.

50
00:02:56,618 --> 00:03:01,687
Many, almost without fail, then
fold everything into consciousness,

51
00:03:01,767 --> 00:03:04,554
much as Yogācāra is commonly read.

52
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:07,570
The producer is gone, the hearer is gone,

53
00:03:07,650 --> 00:03:11,429
and mind is left standing
as what everything is.

54
00:03:11,509 --> 00:03:16,076
The bell, the air and the ear
become contents of one clarity.

55
00:03:16,156 --> 00:03:19,491
That is the ground coming
back, this time as mind.

56
00:03:20,310 --> 00:03:22,404
Here dependency is the key.

57
00:03:22,484 --> 00:03:25,665
The ting is there only with
the bronze, the strike,

58
00:03:25,745 --> 00:03:27,622
the air and the ear.

59
00:03:27,702 --> 00:03:31,168
Being dependent, it is not
mind from its own side,

60
00:03:31,248 --> 00:03:33,994
any more than it is
bronze from its own side.

61
00:03:34,074 --> 00:03:37,173
Clarity is never absent from what appears.

62
00:03:37,253 --> 00:03:40,597
But lifted out, and made
what everything is made of,

63
00:03:40,677 --> 00:03:42,735
it is one more reification.

64
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:47,213
So a phenomenon leans neither
to mind nor to matter.

65
00:03:47,293 --> 00:03:49,414
It is vivid, empty appearing.

66
00:03:49,494 --> 00:03:54,075
The ting, clear and resounding,
arising with its conditions,

67
00:03:54,155 --> 00:03:56,525
and found nowhere when looked for.

68
00:03:57,337 --> 00:04:02,542
When matter is seen through, the habit
does not give up. It changes its stuff.

69
00:04:02,622 --> 00:04:05,191
Matter traded for mind is still stuff.

70
00:04:05,271 --> 00:04:07,773
A phenomenon is not made of anything.

71
00:04:07,853 --> 00:04:10,422
That is what mere convention means to me:

72
00:04:10,502 --> 00:04:13,864
appearing that works, with
no stuff underneath it.

73
00:04:14,669 --> 00:04:17,795
Dependent arising did not
come to me as a theory.

74
00:04:17,875 --> 00:04:21,903
It came as the same seeing
as anatta, turned outwards.

75
00:04:22,713 --> 00:04:26,559
Anatta is the insight that
there is no doer behind seeing.

76
00:04:26,639 --> 00:04:28,665
In seeing, only the seen.

77
00:04:28,745 --> 00:04:30,798
In hearing, only the heard.

78
00:04:30,878 --> 00:04:32,891
The person does not disappear.

79
00:04:32,971 --> 00:04:37,293
What falls away is one picture:
someone standing behind the action,

80
00:04:37,373 --> 00:04:38,573
making it happen.

81
00:04:39,325 --> 00:04:42,492
Nāgārjuna makes the same move everywhere.

82
00:04:42,572 --> 00:04:46,052
A goer does not go, and
a non-goer does not go.

83
00:04:46,132 --> 00:04:51,120
There is no seer behind seeing, no
fire standing apart from its fuel,

84
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:53,352
and no producer behind arising.

85
00:04:54,161 --> 00:04:58,198
Dependent arising is this:
no doer behind anything.

86
00:04:58,278 --> 00:05:02,505
The wind is blowing, and there is
no wind apart from the blowing.

87
00:05:02,585 --> 00:05:05,987
It is raining, and there
is no "it" that rains.

88
00:05:06,789 --> 00:05:11,124
When the witness is not found,
experience does not go blank.

89
00:05:11,204 --> 00:05:13,887
The tree is more vivid, not less.

90
00:05:14,702 --> 00:05:16,742
But anatta does not do everything.

91
00:05:16,822 --> 00:05:19,038
It removes the one who watches.

92
00:05:19,118 --> 00:05:22,883
It does not, by itself,
remove the things watched.

93
00:05:22,963 --> 00:05:26,610
The observer has disappeared,
but the world has not.

94
00:05:26,713 --> 00:05:31,053
Things, causes, time and space
can still be held as solid.

95
00:05:31,853 --> 00:05:35,917
So anatta and dependent
arising are not two subjects.

96
00:05:35,997 --> 00:05:40,034
Anatta, met first, takes
the doer out of seeing.

97
00:05:40,114 --> 00:05:43,525
Dependent arising takes
it out of everything else:

98
00:05:43,605 --> 00:05:47,416
the cause, the object,
the whole, the field.

99
00:05:48,238 --> 00:05:52,914
Then designation. It is not a second
teaching beside dependent arising.

100
00:05:52,994 --> 00:05:56,519
It is the same seeing,
turned on the "this" itself.

101
00:05:57,325 --> 00:05:59,636
Designation does not need words.

102
00:05:59,716 --> 00:06:01,742
It needs only singling out.

103
00:06:01,822 --> 00:06:06,189
This sound, this colour, this
ache, picked out as "this".

104
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:09,636
A "this" stands out only
against what it is not,

105
00:06:09,716 --> 00:06:11,715
and only with these conditions.

106
00:06:11,795 --> 00:06:15,184
In a world of only blue,
no one would see blue.

107
00:06:16,001 --> 00:06:19,779
So the singling out is not done to
an appearance that was there first,

108
00:06:19,859 --> 00:06:22,592
waiting to be named. It is the appearing.

109
00:06:22,672 --> 00:06:26,197
Because it is already
dependence, it is already empty.

110
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:29,294
The clearest case is the oldest.

111
00:06:29,374 --> 00:06:33,126
Nāgasena asks King Milinda
where his chariot is.

112
00:06:33,206 --> 00:06:37,827
It is not the pole, not the axle,
not the wheels, not the frame.

113
00:06:37,907 --> 00:06:40,861
Not their sum, and not
something apart from them.

114
00:06:41,665 --> 00:06:45,933
Candrakīrti makes the search
complete, in seven ways.

115
00:06:46,013 --> 00:06:50,158
The chariot is not the same as its
parts, and not other than them.

116
00:06:50,238 --> 00:06:54,438
It does not possess them, is not
in them, and does not contain them.

117
00:06:54,518 --> 00:06:58,546
It is not their collection, and
not their shape. Nothing is found.

118
00:06:59,357 --> 00:07:04,589
Yet the chariot is not denied. It carries
you to town. Walking is the chariot.

119
00:07:04,669 --> 00:07:06,306
Hearing is the chariot.

120
00:07:07,113 --> 00:07:09,478
And the basis is designated too.

121
00:07:09,558 --> 00:07:12,277
The chariot is designated on its wheels.

122
00:07:12,357 --> 00:07:16,652
But a wheel is singled out in
turn, on rim, spokes and hub.

123
00:07:16,732 --> 00:07:19,506
They on their wood, and
the wood on its grain.

124
00:07:19,586 --> 00:07:24,709
No bottom layer is ever reached, where
something finally stands by itself and

125
00:07:24,789 --> 00:07:26,544
receives the first name.

126
00:07:26,624 --> 00:07:28,817
There is nowhere for the search to end.

127
00:07:29,629 --> 00:07:34,426
Now, the Buddhist tradition itself
once set out to find that bottom layer.

128
00:07:34,506 --> 00:07:38,367
The Abhidharma, above all
the Sarvāstivāda school,

129
00:07:38,447 --> 00:07:40,799
tried to list what is finally there.

130
00:07:40,879 --> 00:07:45,772
Tables, people and chariots,
it said, are only designated.

131
00:07:45,852 --> 00:07:48,072
Take them apart, and they are gone.

132
00:07:48,881 --> 00:07:51,586
What the analysis comes
down to are the dharmas,

133
00:07:51,666 --> 00:07:53,896
the last units of experience.

134
00:07:53,976 --> 00:07:58,828
A moment of hardness, of
heat, of sound, of feeling.

135
00:07:58,908 --> 00:08:04,113
Each is defined by its own mark,
its svalakṣaṇa. Earth by hardness.

136
00:08:04,193 --> 00:08:05,667
Water by cohesion.

137
00:08:05,769 --> 00:08:08,751
Fire by heat. Space by not obstructing.

138
00:08:09,573 --> 00:08:15,172
In the Abhidharma's own gloss, a dharma is
so called because it bears its own mark.

139
00:08:15,252 --> 00:08:18,732
And that mark is its own
nature, its svabhāva,

140
00:08:18,812 --> 00:08:22,998
there from its own side, whether
or not anyone designates it.

141
00:08:23,078 --> 00:08:26,630
So the chariot was designated,
but its floor was not.

142
00:08:27,433 --> 00:08:30,777
Nāgārjuna aims at exactly this definition.

143
00:08:30,857 --> 00:08:34,785
In chapter 5 of his Middle
Way verses, he takes space,

144
00:08:34,865 --> 00:08:38,956
the hardest case, since some
schools held it to be unconditioned.

145
00:08:39,036 --> 00:08:41,143
Can space be there before its mark?

146
00:08:41,223 --> 00:08:45,845
He answers: "No space at all is found
before the defining characteristic of

147
00:08:45,925 --> 00:08:50,274
space." Space without its mark
would be a thing with no mark,

148
00:08:50,354 --> 00:08:52,697
and no such thing is found anywhere.

149
00:08:53,501 --> 00:08:55,567
Then the mark must apply to something.

150
00:08:55,647 --> 00:09:00,228
But it cannot apply to what has no
mark, nor to what already has one,

151
00:09:00,308 --> 00:09:02,673
and there is nowhere else for it to apply.

152
00:09:02,753 --> 00:09:06,020
So mark and marked stand or fall together.

153
00:09:06,204 --> 00:09:11,070
"The characterised is not found, and
the characteristic is not found."

154
00:09:11,150 --> 00:09:14,793
Neither comes first. Each is
set up only with the other.

155
00:09:14,873 --> 00:09:16,931
Which is to say, designated.

156
00:09:17,745 --> 00:09:20,504
Chapter 15 shows why it had to be so.

157
00:09:20,584 --> 00:09:26,584
Own nature, by definition, "is not made,
and does not depend on anything else."

158
00:09:26,807 --> 00:09:30,763
But the dharmas were said to
arise from causes and conditions.

159
00:09:30,843 --> 00:09:35,097
And "own nature that came about from
causes and conditions would be something

160
00:09:35,177 --> 00:09:36,377
made."

161
00:09:36,805 --> 00:09:39,741
A dharma with its own
nature could not arise,

162
00:09:39,821 --> 00:09:42,707
could not change, and could not cease.

163
00:09:42,797 --> 00:09:45,937
"A nature becoming otherwise
never makes sense."

164
00:09:46,017 --> 00:09:49,958
Grant the dharmas their own
nature, and dependent arising,

165
00:09:50,038 --> 00:09:52,748
the Buddha's own teaching, stops working.

166
00:09:53,561 --> 00:09:57,860
None of this denies that fire
burns, or that earth is solid.

167
00:09:57,976 --> 00:10:01,945
Fire is still hot. The marks
keep working, by convention.

168
00:10:02,025 --> 00:10:04,011
A doctor still reads a fever.

169
00:10:04,091 --> 00:10:06,049
A builder still tests a beam.

170
00:10:06,129 --> 00:10:09,744
What goes is their standing
as the final building blocks.

171
00:10:09,824 --> 00:10:15,179
And Nāgārjuna does not put a better
definition of a phenomenon in their place.

172
00:10:15,259 --> 00:10:19,269
He shows that any attempt to
ground things in self-contained,

173
00:10:19,349 --> 00:10:22,385
uniquely marked units is reification.

174
00:10:23,205 --> 00:10:25,176
This is where the apple comes back.

175
00:10:25,256 --> 00:10:28,410
The hardness in my palm looks
like the last thing left,

176
00:10:28,490 --> 00:10:30,421
once the apple is seen through.

177
00:10:30,501 --> 00:10:32,880
Earth's own mark, found at last.

178
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:36,848
But hardness is singled out
on touch, skin and pressure.

179
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:39,388
It stands out only against softness.

180
00:10:39,468 --> 00:10:43,356
It arises with the hand that
meets it, and the knowing of it.

181
00:10:43,436 --> 00:10:46,689
It is not a mark that something
carries from its own side.

182
00:10:47,524 --> 00:10:50,338
For me, a phenomenon is just this.

183
00:10:50,418 --> 00:10:53,653
Vividly appearing,
singled out in dependence,

184
00:10:53,733 --> 00:10:56,900
its mark and what it
marks designated together,

185
00:10:56,980 --> 00:10:59,210
and nothing found that holds it there.

186
00:10:59,290 --> 00:11:03,495
The dharmas were meant to be the
bottom layer. They are designated too.

187
00:11:04,328 --> 00:11:06,558
Here is where the expression is hardest.

188
00:11:06,638 --> 00:11:10,308
The chariot is not found,
and still we ride it to town.

189
00:11:10,388 --> 00:11:13,229
So what is a chariot that
is merely designated?

190
00:11:13,309 --> 00:11:18,179
It is not only a name, and it is not
only in the mind. Four points hold it.

191
00:11:19,074 --> 00:11:22,771
First, designation and
functioning arise together.

192
00:11:22,851 --> 00:11:26,100
We do not first have a name
and then stick it on a heap.

193
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:29,116
The chariot is called a
chariot because it carries.

194
00:11:29,196 --> 00:11:31,155
That is why the name is not free.

195
00:11:31,235 --> 00:11:36,127
You cannot point at a heap of sand,
call it a chariot, and ride it to town.

196
00:11:36,207 --> 00:11:39,121
A designation holds only where it works.

197
00:11:39,938 --> 00:11:44,618
Second, the search removes only a
chariot standing from its own side:

198
00:11:44,707 --> 00:11:48,921
a chariot inside the parts, or
a power that makes them carry.

199
00:11:49,001 --> 00:11:52,453
That was never found, and
the carrying never needed it.

200
00:11:52,533 --> 00:11:55,990
The wheels turn, the
load moves, you arrive.

201
00:11:56,855 --> 00:11:59,510
Third, it is not only in the mind.

202
00:11:59,654 --> 00:12:02,903
"Just a label in the mind"
sounds like the humble answer.

203
00:12:02,983 --> 00:12:05,892
But it quietly sets up
a mind that is found,

204
00:12:05,972 --> 00:12:09,655
standing behind and
painting names onto a world.

205
00:12:09,735 --> 00:12:11,517
That mind is singled out too.

206
00:12:11,597 --> 00:12:13,569
No labeller stands behind it.

207
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:17,975
So the chariot is no more made of
mind than it is made of chariot stuff.

208
00:12:18,843 --> 00:12:23,573
Fourth, the basis has no bottom layer,
and functioning never needed one.

209
00:12:23,653 --> 00:12:27,948
Because nothing stands by itself,
the chariot can be put together,

210
00:12:28,028 --> 00:12:31,281
carry you, break down and be mended.

211
00:12:32,089 --> 00:12:37,321
In one line: being unfound removes
the chariot that stands by itself,

212
00:12:37,401 --> 00:12:40,614
and leaves the chariot
that carries you, whole.

213
00:12:41,442 --> 00:12:44,940
Two pictures creep back, once
the things are seen through.

214
00:12:45,766 --> 00:12:48,037
The first puts the conditions underneath,

215
00:12:48,117 --> 00:12:52,249
as parts lined up below that then
produce the appearing on top.

216
00:12:52,329 --> 00:12:57,140
But the conditions are the appearing, cut
into parts by a framework for explaining

217
00:12:57,220 --> 00:12:58,689
and getting things done.

218
00:12:58,769 --> 00:13:03,173
The cook, the chemist and the physicist
cut the same loaf differently.

219
00:13:03,253 --> 00:13:05,496
Each cut works within its own setting.

220
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:07,715
None is the loaf from its own side.

221
00:13:08,546 --> 00:13:11,646
The second keeps the relations
when the things are gone.

222
00:13:11,726 --> 00:13:14,159
A web, a network, a field.

223
00:13:14,239 --> 00:13:16,990
But the line is as unfindable as the dot.

224
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:20,029
"Coming into contact,
having come into contact,

225
00:13:20,109 --> 00:13:23,697
and the one who brings them
into contact are not found."

226
00:13:23,777 --> 00:13:28,457
Relation and what it relates are
designated together. Neither is prior.

227
00:13:29,273 --> 00:13:34,451
Indra's net is a fine image, so long as
the net itself is not taken as what is

228
00:13:34,531 --> 00:13:37,875
finally found. And the
order is fully valid.

229
00:13:37,955 --> 00:13:42,567
It is not a hidden code, or a set
of laws standing behind appearing.

230
00:13:43,365 --> 00:13:46,654
So "nothing stands alone"
is only half of it.

231
00:13:46,734 --> 00:13:51,450
The other half is that the relations are
not found from their own side either.

232
00:13:51,530 --> 00:13:53,176
What is left is not a web.

233
00:13:53,256 --> 00:13:54,947
It is this, appearing.

234
00:13:55,753 --> 00:13:58,811
All views and understanding
